CMSIS-RTOS v1: osPriorityNormal = 0. makeFreeRtosPriority typically = tpriority + osPriorityIdle... Actually in cmsis_os.c there's usually `#define makeFreeRtosPriority(p)  (p - osPriorityIdle - 1)`? Hmm, let me think — actually in the classic cmsis_os.c:

```c
#define makeFreeRtosPriority(p)  ((tskPriority) (p))
```

Hmm no. In the STM32 CubeMX cmsis_os.c (v1):

```c
/* Initialization parameters for tasks */
...
#define makeFreeRtosPriority(p)  ((int)(p)) - osPriorityIdle - 1 ??? 
```

Actually I remember in CubeMX's cmsis_os.c (the one shipped with FreeRTOS v10.x / CMSIS-RTOS v1):

```c
static inline uint32_t makeFreeRtosPriority (osPriority priority)
{
  uint32_t fpriority = tskIDLE_PRIORITY;

  if (priority != osPriorityError) {
    /* Map the priority to FreeRTOS priority */
    fpriority += (priority - osPriorityIdle);
  }

  return fpriority;
}
```

So osPriorityIdle (-3) → tskIDLE_PRIORITY (0), osPriorityNormal (0) → tskIDLE_PRIORITY + 3 = 3. osPriorityRealtime (+3) → 6.

So defaultTask = FreeRTOS priority 3 (with configMAX_PRIORITIES=7), LedStatusTask = priority 6. So LED task has higher priority than the main task. And configMAX_PRIORITIES = 7 means 0-6 valid; priority 6 = highest, used by LedStatusTask. Good — I can state: defaultTask 运行在 FreeRTOS 优先级 3（tskIDLE_PRIORITY + 3），LedStatusTask 在优先级 6（最高）。That claim follows from the standard makeFreeRtosPriority mapping in CubeMX's cmsis_os.c. Let me verify the makeFreeRtosPriority in this specific file to be safe.

